  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Divide these polynomials and express in the form $\\frac{P(x)}{D(x)}=Q(x)+\\frac{R(x)}{D(x)}$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(-2x^3-2x^2-5x+7)\\div(x+4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2x^2+6x-29+\\frac{123}{x+4}$. Quotient $-2x^2+6x-29$; remainder $123$.",
          "worked": "Successive quotient terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{-2x^3}{x}&=-2x^2\\\\\\frac{6x^2}{x}&=6x\\\\\\frac{-29x}{x}&=-29\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract each divisor multiple:\n$$\\begin{align*}(-2x^3-2x^2-5x+7)-(-2x^3-8x^2)&=6x^2-5x+7\\\\(6x^2-5x+7)-(6x^2+24x)&=-29x+7\\\\(-29x+7)-(-29x-116)&=123\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\frac{-2x^3-2x^2-5x+7}{x+4}=-2x^2+6x-29+\\frac{123}{x+4}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(-5x^3+11x^2-2x-20)\\div(x-3)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-5x^2-4x-14-\\frac{62}{x-3}$. Quotient $-5x^2-4x-14$; remainder $-62$.",
          "worked": "Successive quotient terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{-5x^3}{x}&=-5x^2\\\\\\frac{-4x^2}{x}&=-4x\\\\\\frac{-14x}{x}&=-14\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract each divisor multiple:\n$$\\begin{align*}(-5x^3+11x^2-2x-20)-(-5x^3+15x^2)&=-4x^2-2x-20\\\\(-4x^2-2x-20)-(-4x^2+12x)&=-14x-20\\\\(-14x-20)-(-14x+42)&=-62\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\frac{-5x^3+11x^2-2x-20}{x-3}=-5x^2-4x-14+\\frac{-62}{x-3}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(6x^4-5x^3+9x^2-8x+2)\\div(2x-1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3x^3-x^2+4x-2$. Quotient $3x^3-x^2+4x-2$; remainder $0$.",
          "worked": "Successive quotient terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6x^4}{2x}&=3x^3\\\\\\frac{-2x^3}{2x}&=-x^2\\\\\\frac{8x^2}{2x}&=4x\\\\\\frac{-4x}{2x}&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract each divisor multiple:\n$$\\begin{align*}(6x^4-5x^3+9x^2-8x+2)-(6x^4-3x^3)&=-2x^3+9x^2-8x+2\\\\(-2x^3+9x^2-8x+2)-(-2x^3+x^2)&=8x^2-8x+2\\\\(8x^2-8x+2)-(8x^2-4x)&=-4x+2\\\\(-4x+2)-(-4x+2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\frac{6x^4-5x^3+9x^2-8x+2}{2x-1}=3x^3-x^2+4x-2.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 82
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(10x^4-x^3+3x^2-3x-2)\\div(5x+2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x^3-x^2+x-1$. Quotient $2x^3-x^2+x-1$; remainder $0$.",
          "worked": "Successive quotient terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{10x^4}{5x}&=2x^3\\\\\\frac{-5x^3}{5x}&=-x^2\\\\\\frac{5x^2}{5x}&=x\\\\\\frac{-5x}{5x}&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract each divisor multiple:\n$$\\begin{align*}(10x^4-x^3+3x^2-3x-2)-(10x^4+4x^3)&=-5x^3+3x^2-3x-2\\\\(-5x^3+3x^2-3x-2)-(-5x^3-2x^2)&=5x^2-3x-2\\\\(5x^2-3x-2)-(5x^2+2x)&=-5x-2\\\\(-5x-2)-(-5x-2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\frac{10x^4-x^3+3x^2-3x-2}{5x+2}=2x^3-x^2+x-1.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 82
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(x^3-5x+3)\\div(x-2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2+2x-1+\\frac{1}{x-2}$. Quotient $x^2+2x-1$; remainder $1$.",
          "worked": "Include the missing $x^2$ term as $0x^2$. Successive quotient terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^3}{x}&=x^2\\\\\\frac{2x^2}{x}&=2x\\\\\\frac{-x}{x}&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract each divisor multiple:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^3+0x^2-5x+3)-(x^3-2x^2)&=2x^2-5x+3\\\\(2x^2-5x+3)-(2x^2-4x)&=-x+3\\\\(-x+3)-(-x+2)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\frac{x^3-5x+3}{x-2}=x^2+2x-1+\\frac{1}{x-2}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$(x^3-3x-2)\\div(x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^2-x-2$. Quotient $x^2-x-2$; remainder $0$.",
          "worked": "Include the missing $x^2$ term as $0x^2$. Successive quotient terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^3}{x}&=x^2\\\\\\frac{-x^2}{x}&=-x\\\\\\frac{-2x}{x}&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract each divisor multiple:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^3+0x^2-3x-2)-(x^3+x^2)&=-x^2-3x-2\\\\(-x^2-3x-2)-(-x^2-x)&=-2x-2\\\\(-2x-2)-(-2x-2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\frac{x^3-3x-2}{x+1}=x^2-x-2.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
